---
description: Block agent access to .env and other secret files (even via Shell)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Env / credential files — agent must not access

`.cursorignore` is **not** a security boundary. Shell with elevated permissions can still read ignored files.

## Never do this

- ❌ Read, write, append, or search dotenv files, PEM/key files, or credentials JSON
- ❌ Use Shell (`cat`, `rg`, `printf >>`, `sed`, etc.) to touch those paths
- ❌ Request `required_permissions: ["all"]` in order to bypass ignore/sandbox for those files
- ❌ Paste values from those files into chat

## Do this instead

- ✅ Tell the user which env **key name** to set (e.g. `CONNECTION_LIMIT_API=25`) and ask them to edit the local env file
- ✅ Use committed examples only (`*.example`, docs) — never real values
- ✅ If a task requires changing the local env file, stop and ask the user to make the change
